+# Hotbar: Figma to Roblox notes
+
+Source: `design/figma/hotbar.json`, which is the Figma file "Block Builder - UI" exported with
+`GET /v1/files/:key/nodes`. It contains frame **HUD / Desktop** (`31:100`) and the component set
+**Hotbar Slot** (`31:2`), which has the variants Default, Hover, Pressed and Selected.
+Implementation: `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Hotbar.luau`.
+
+No screenshot came with the export, so everything here is based on the node data alone. Nobody
+has compared the result with the Figma frame side by side yet.
+
+## Matched exactly
+
+These values come straight from the node data. They are in pixels for the 1080-tall reference
+screen, and `Screen.luau` scales them up on larger screens.
+
+- **Placement:** the bar's bottom edge is 24 px above the bottom of the screen and it is centered
+  horizontally. The selected-name label sits 8 px above the bar.
+- **Bar:** 732 × 84 for 10 slots, with 10 px padding, 8 px between slots, corner radius 14, fill
+  `#0E1020` and 80% opacity.
+- **Slot:** 64 × 64, corner radius 12. The fill is `#262B45` by default, `#313858` on Hover and
+  `#1D2136` on Pressed.
+- **Selected stroke:** 3 px, drawn outside the slot (UIStroke's default for borders), with a
+  left-to-right gradient from `#FFD25A` to `#FF801A`. I used a UIGradient parented to the
+  UIStroke.
+- **Swatch:** 40 × 40, corner radius 8, centered in the slot. Its color is the block's `Color`
+  from `BlockTypes`, as the component description says. The brick red in the file is only
+  placeholder data.
+- **Key badge:** an 18 × 18 circle at (4, 4), black at 55%. The key number is Builder Sans Bold
+  12, white and centered. It is hidden for slots that have no number key, which stands in for the
+  "Show Key" property.
+- **Pressed variant:** the slot shrinks to 60 × 60, the swatch to 36 × 36, and the badge moves
+  to (3, 3).
+- **Selected name:** 22 px white text in a 28 px tall row. It sizes to fit the text, which
+  matches `textAutoResize`.
+- **Bar opacity:** the 80% applies to the whole bar as one layer. I did this with a
+  `CanvasGroup` (`GroupTransparency = 0.2`), so the bar does not show through the slots and
+  swatches.
+
+## Not reproducible exactly, and what I used instead
+
+| Design | Why Roblox can't match it | What I used |
+|---|---|---|
+| Selected name in **Gilroy ExtraBold** | Gilroy isn't one of Roblox's fonts, and games can't upload their own fonts. | **Builder Sans ExtraBold** (weight 800), the same size and weight. The letter shapes differ, and Builder Sans runs a bit wider. |
+| Selected name **letter spacing −0.5 px** | TextLabels have no letter-spacing setting, and RichText doesn't offer one either. | Default spacing. "Brick" comes out about 2 px wider than in the design. |
+| Selected name **2 px outside stroke, black at 60%** | UIStroke on text doesn't let you choose inside, center or outside. | `UIStroke` with `Contextual` mode, thickness 2, transparency 0.4. It should look very close, but the outline may sit slightly differently on the glyph edges. |
+| Slot **corner smoothing 0.6** (iOS-style squircle) | UICorner only draws circular arcs. | `UICorner` with radius 12, so the corners look a little sharper where the curve meets the straight edge. Getting the smoothing exactly would need a 9-slice image. |
+| Bar **top-only inside stroke** (2 px, white at 12%; the other sides are 0) | UIStroke draws the same width on every side, so a single side isn't possible. | A 2 px white frame at 88% transparency along the top edge of the bar. The CanvasGroup's rounded corners clip its ends. In Figma the stroke follows the corner curves and tapers off down the sides; this version stops where the corner clipping cuts it. |
+| **Separate variants** Default / Hover / Pressed / Selected | The variants can't all be active at once in Figma, but in the game a slot can be selected and hovered (or pressed) at the same time. The design doesn't show those combinations. | Two separate pieces: the fill and size follow the pointer (Hover or Pressed), and the gradient stroke shows whenever the slot is selected. So a selected slot under the cursor gets the Hover fill plus the gold stroke. **Designer: please confirm, or add Selected+Hover and Selected+Pressed variants.** |
+| **Pressed variant is 60 × 60** and anchored top-left in the component set | If the slot shrank within the row, every slot after it would shift by 4 px. | Each slot keeps a fixed 64 × 64 hit area, and the visible body shrinks around its center. The swatch inset (12 px) matches the variant. |
+| **Hover / Pressed** as static frames | Figma doesn't say when these states apply or how they animate. | The states follow the button's `GuiState`. Hover shows only with a mouse; touch goes straight to Pressed. States switch instantly with no tweening, because the file has no prototype transitions. |
+| **CanvasGroup** for the 80% bar opacity (see above) | This is a faithful match, but CanvasGroups draw to a texture, which costs memory and can look slightly soft on some low-end devices. | If that becomes a problem, drop the CanvasGroup and set 0.2 transparency on each element instead. The bar would then show through the slots a little. |
+
+## Behavior kept as before
+
+- Clicking or tapping a slot selects that block (`Activated` calls `BlockPlacer.setBlockType`).
+  Because the slot is a GuiButton, the click doesn't also place a block in the world.
+- Keys 1–9 and 0 still select blocks. `BlockPlacer` handles them, and the hotbar shows the change
+  through the `Selected` source. The module's interface (`Selected`, `Select`) hasn't changed, so
+  `Main.client.luau` needed no edits.
+- I turned off `AutoButtonColor` because the design now defines the Hover and Pressed colors. The
+  button's leftover "Button" text is now cleared.
